  <page_number>382</page_number>
  <running_head>Castigatio Paral.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">rodoxa &amp; fidei catholica contraria.</l>
    <l n="2">His iterum respondit Prosper &amp; dixit</l>
    <l n="3">illos calumniatores Augustinum cele-</l>
    <l n="4">berrimi nominis virum, promptius cul-</l>
    <l n="5">pare quàm nosse. Compellarunt etiam</l>
    <l n="6">Prosper &amp; Hilarius Cælestinum pri-</l>
    <l n="7">mum Pontificem Romanum, &amp; roga-</l>
    <l n="8">runt ut doctrinæ Augustinianæ patroci-</l>
    <l n="9">nium susciperet, quod Papa fecit in</l>
    <l n="10">epistola ad quosdam Galliarum Episco-</l>
    <l n="11">pos, in qua Augustini sententiam &amp;</l>
    <l n="12">Prosperi ac Hilarii defensionem appro-</l>
    <l n="13">bavit.</l>
    <l n="14" para="true">Haud multò post, Faustus Abbas</l>
    <l n="15">Rhegiensis Semipelagianorum opinio-</l>
    <l n="16">ni sese associans doctrinam ab Augu-</l>
    <l n="17">stino propositam, &amp; à Prospero, Hila-</l>
    <l n="18">rio &amp; Cælestino defensam, publico</l>
    <l n="19">scripto damnavit &amp; hærefin appellavit</l>
    <l n="20">primus. Gennadius Massiliensis, qui</l>
    <l n="21">vixit A. D. 490. Fausti doctrinam lau-</l>
    <l n="22">davit, &amp; Augustinianam doctrinam</l>
    <l n="23">(suppresso Augustini nomine) hærefin</l>
    <l n="24">Præde-</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Catchword "Præde-" appears at the foot right; it is the start of the next page's word and is included in the text above as the last word. Page number "382" printed top left. Running head "Castigatio Paral." printed top right.</notes>
</page>
